{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/281618-resistors-wound-healing","id":281618,"title":"Resistors+Wound Healing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-14T16:50:12-07:00","id":281618,"title":"Resistors+Wound Healing","content":"I have been lurking on this forum for a while and I have wanted to join for a while.<br /> I would like to know how you guess would run someone having Resistors and Wound Healing and what you think the intent was.<br /> Resistors ignores the first source of damage you gain and doesn't come back until you completely get your health back and wound healing would mean you would heal the resistor back each turn.<br /> Not that i mind it just means you would have to gang up on the person, but since nWoD does not to multiple actions that one and one fights will go one way. Unless you come up with some clever thinking like grabbing someone and flying up and shooting them as they fall so they take the falling damage there etc<br /> <br /> Thanks for any help you can give","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T17:01:44-07:00","id":281642,"title":"","content":"It's an awkward combination of power triggers, yeah, although technically you would need to then get hit a second time and finish healing it with Wound Healing before the Resistors would come back. Resistor shortage isn't a point of damage, so you can't regenerate your Health until you've actually taken damage. How difficult this is would depend on how hard the subsequent hits are.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd probably also house-rule patch it to require a minimum of one scene cooldown before the Resistors recover. That'd make Wound Healing recover them quickly while still keeping Resistors' role as a once-per-encounter alpha strike defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T04:25:45-07:00","id":283706,"title":"","content":"Yeah the way I am running it is the why you described it first. Wound Healing do not activate as you have not taken damage, so the resistors do not reform. Without this ruling all the demon needs now is just bruised and as long as he can keep up the embed rolls he is unkillable in a one and one fight.<br /> <br /> I am not worried too much about having a demon like that, it can make plot much more interesting as others find out a way to deal with him in combat. I think it would be quite cool to have the &quot;why won\u2019t you die&quot; character being a PC instead of a NPC and the more crazy things people try and do to try and kill him.<br /> <br /> Layered explosions? I will let resistors take the first one, Just bruised the second with using playing possum. Best thing they think I'm dead. He can still be one shot in his cover without his demonic form abilities anyway.<br /> I am just a new GM for a group of quite experienced role players, and I am not running to have an arms race with my players but tell a story I hope they will like.<br /> <br /> Also If I was a demon trying to kill someone myself is the last thing I would want to do, I would just tip off the right person (or angel) or break their cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T14:58:18-07:00","id":284247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mental-State</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/281618-resistors-wound-healing?p=283706#post283706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah the way I am running it is the why you described it first. Wound Healing do not activate as you have not taken damage, so the resistors do not reform. Without this ruling all the demon needs now is just bruised and as long as he can keep up the embed rolls he is unkillable in a one and one fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Environmental Tilts that produce ongoing damage or retard the healing processes of beings within them.<br /> <br /> Demon has at least two Exploits and two Form Abilities that can produce these conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T04:54:11-07:00","id":284850,"title":"","content":"Thanks Satchel, it is good to know what things can deal with such a thing but I am not the kind of person to build a NPC with the only reason to get around a players power combo, but that doesn't mean after a few botched murder attempts that someone wouldn't look for the right person for the job.<br /> <br /> But Satchel how do you think it was meant to be ruled and how would you rule it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T14:35:03-07:00","id":285418,"title":"","content":"Resistors break and you have to take damage for them to refresh, which, with Wound Healing in play, means the fight just became an Aggravated Damage Party or at the very least a time to break out the plagues of locusts and rains of blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}